        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0650" n="516" xml:id="pg516"/>

                <head>No. 368.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McLane to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-24"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 24, 1888</date>.
                        (Received March 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 554.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 287 of January 12,
                    1888, instructing me to obtain from the French foreign office a statement of the
                    relations now subsisting between the French Republic and the King of Johanna (or
                    Anjouan), one of the Comoro Islands, I inclose a copy and a translation of a
                    note from Mr. Flourens, stating that the French Republic has assumed the
                    protectorate of that island by virtue of two treaties, signed April 21, 1886,
                    and October 15, 1887. A copy and a translation of those treaties are also
                    herewith inclosed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert M. McLane</hi></signed></closer>




